NOAA's Rapid Refresh forecast (RAP, 13 km, the contiguous U.S. and nearby Canada and Mexico) at a site, from NOAA's NOMADS server

Usage: hpr weather rap [OPTIONS] --latitude <DEG> --longitude <DEG>

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text, errors included

      --latitude <DEG>
          The site's latitude, degrees north (south is negative)

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. With auto, output to a terminal is colored, and NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE are followed. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --longitude <DEG>
          The site's longitude, degrees east (west is negative)

      --cycle <TIME>
          The run to read, by its start in UTC, such as 2026-09-30T00Z; needed unless --from is given

      --hour <HOUR>
          How many hours after the run's start the forecast is for; needed unless --from is given

      --from <FILE>
          Read the source's answer from this file, saved earlier, instead of fetching it

      --offline
          Answer from the cache only, never the network

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write the profile to this file, as JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Read a RAP answer saved earlier, at a site:
      hpr weather rap --latitude 40.865 --longitude -119.063 --from rap.grib2
  Fetch one run's forecast for 3 hours after its start:
      hpr weather rap --latitude 40.865 --longitude -119.063 --cycle 2026-09-26T12Z --hour 3

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-weather
